---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy — StudyRoadmap Cookies & Ads" description="StudyRoadmap privacy policy: Google Analytics, local storage, Google AdSense cookies, DoubleClick DART, Consent Mode, and how to opt out of personalised ads.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://studyroadmap.in/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Privacy Policy","item":"https://studyroadmap.in/privacy/"}]})}>
  </script>
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-surface-50 dark:bg-surface-950 border-b border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
      <div class="container-page py-14 text-center">
        <h1 class="heading-1 text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-50">Privacy Policy</h1>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="container-page py-14 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 leading-relaxed">
        <p><strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Effective date:</strong> 26 July 2026</p>
        <p>StudyRoadmap™ is built with privacy as a core principle. We collect <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">as little data as possible</strong> while still understanding how the site is used.</p>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">What We Collect</h2>
          <p>We use <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Google Analytics 4</strong> (measurement ID <code class="text-xs">G-XPWXLW8J3R</code>) to measure aggregated traffic and page performance. GA4 may process technical data such as approximate location (city/country derived from IP), device/browser type, pages viewed, referrers, and session duration. We do not use GA4 to identify you by name, and we do not upload student lists or exam choices to Google Analytics. IP anonymization is enabled in our GA configuration.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Our self-hosted nginx server also logs standard request metadata (IP, user-agent, referrer) in access logs for security and operations. We do not sell personal data. Exam selection and study-plan preferences stay in your browser's local storage and are not sent to our servers as account data.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Consent Mode (EEA, UK, Switzerland)</h2>
          <p>We implement <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Google Consent Mode v2</strong> defaults before the analytics tag loads. For visitors in the EEA, United Kingdom, and Switzerland, <code class="text-xs">analytics_storage</code> defaults to denied so GA4 runs in a limited, cookieless measurement mode unless a future consent update grants storage. Advertising storage signals (<code class="text-xs">ad_storage</code>, <code class="text-xs">ad_user_data</code>, <code class="text-xs">ad_personalization</code>) default to denied for all regions until Google AdSense (or another ad network) is enabled with an appropriate consent experience. Outside those regions, analytics storage defaults to granted for aggregated site measurement only.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
          <p>We use your browser's <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">local storage</strong> to save exam selection and duration preferences. That data stays on your device. Google Analytics and (when enabled) advertising partners may set first- or third-party cookies or use similar storage for analytics and ad measurement. You can clear cookies and local storage anytime in browser settings. For Google ad personalisation opt-out, see the Advertising section below. You can also use browser controls or Google's tools described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Your Data Rights</h2>
          <p>Depending on where you live (including the EEA, UK, Switzerland, and India), you may have rights to access, correct, erase, restrict, port, or object to processing of personal data. Analytics data held by Google is governed by Google's terms and privacy policy; we will help route legitimate requests. For concerns about our server access logs or this policy, contact us at the addresses below.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>We self-host the site on an <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">nginx</strong> server and use <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Google Fonts</strong> (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com) for typography and <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Google Analytics 4</strong> (googletagmanager.com / google-analytics.com) for traffic measurement. Google receives technical request data governed by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a>. When we display ads via <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Google AdSense</strong>, EEA, UK, and Swiss visitors will see a Google-provided consent prompt for personalised advertising in line with UK/EU GDPR. You retain the right to access, correct, erase, restrict, port, or object to processing of any personal data held by these providers — contact us at the email below and we will route the request.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
          <p>We may display advertisements through third-party advertising networks such as <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Google AdSense</strong>. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our users based on their visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Google may use the <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">DoubleClick DART cookie</strong> and similar technologies for interest-based advertising and to measure ad performance. Users may opt out of the use of the DART cookie by visiting the <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Ads Settings</a> page. You may also opt out of personalised advertising from participating companies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">aboutads.info/choices</a> or the EU industry page at <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Third-party vendors and ad networks that serve ads on StudyRoadmap may be listed at Google's <a href="https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/94149" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">AdSense partner information</a> and may set their own cookies subject to their policies. We do not sell personal information collected for advertising. Ad placement does not change editorial study recommendations.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">When AdSense is enabled for visitors in the EEA, UK, or Switzerland, Google's consent messaging may request permission before using personalised advertising cookies, consistent with Consent Mode defaults described above.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>Our site is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect any information from anyone under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided personal information through our site, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy occasionally. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">Contact</h2>
          <p>If you have questions about this privacy policy, reach out to us:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
            <li>
              <a href="mailto:pushkersaini@gmail.com" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-400">
                pushkersaini@gmail.com
              </a>
              — for privacy questions and data requests
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/feedback/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-400">
                Submit feedback
              </a>
              — for bug reports and feature suggestions
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
